Author: Eason Liang <easonliang28@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 25 23:29:10 2026 +0800

    fix(webview): route focusInput to the focused surface and type the profile-deletion not-found signal
    
    Address the pre-merge review findings on the viewstate-loaded unit that
    were still open after the re-stack onto the fixed F6 head:
    
    - Route the zoo-code.focusInput post to the surface focusPanel selected:
      the tracked tab's provider when a tab panel is tracked, otherwise the
      sidebar registration (previously the post was dropped while any tab
      panel was tracked).
    - Log a rejected webview postMessage instead of swallowing the rejection
      silently.
    - Replace the "not found" message-substring check in deleteProviderProfile
      with a typed ProviderConfigNotFoundError raised by
      ProviderSettingsManager.deleteConfig, so an unrelated failure whose
      message merely mentions "not found" propagates to the caller.
    - Test quality: assert the posted state payload in the API-config-locking
      mode-switch test; cover the unrelated-pin and no-pin-unrelated-deletion
      branches of deleteProviderProfile; assert the updateSettings path
      routes changed keys through provider.setValue; rename the
      api-task-control review-fixes describe to its subjects; split the
      persisted-view-state lifecycle tests out of the getState merging
      block.
    
    Tests:
    - registerCommands: focusInput posts to the tracked tab provider while a
      tab panel is tracked; posts nothing and logs nothing when the tracked
      tab has no live provider; the sidebar-only and no-panel cases are
      unchanged.
    - ProviderSettingsManager: a missing profile rejects with the typed
      ProviderConfigNotFoundError identity (instanceof, name, message).
    - ClineProvider: a rejected postMessage is logged; the typed not-found
      signal is an idempotent prune; a wrapped failure containing the
      "not found" substring propagates; an unrelated deletion with no view
      pin skips the activation path.
    - sticky-profile: an unrelated view-local pin survives deletion of a
      different profile while the other view's persisted pin is re-pointed
      at the replacement.
    - webviewMessageHandler: updateSettings routes a changed key through
      provider.setValue before posting state.
    - parallelMode: the locked mode switch posts the switched state payload.
    
    Mutation gate: local Stryker preflight (unit delta 453938c..f57fe9008) kills
    all mutants (extension: 20 valid / 20 killed / 0 timeout / 0 survived / 0
    noCoverage; webview: 7 valid / 7 killed / 0 timeout / 0 survived / 0
    noCoverage) - the first run surfaced 2 blocking survivors (the focusInput
    no-live-provider guard and the ProviderConfigNotFoundError name), each
    killed by the tests above.
    
    Validation: vitest 492/492 across the seven touched suites (registerCommands,
    ProviderSettingsManager, ClineProvider, ClineProvider.parallelMode,
    ClineProvider.sticky-profile, webviewMessageHandler, api-task-control); the two
    kill-test suites re-run green after the kill tests landed; tsc --noEmit 0;
    eslint clean (suppression counts unchanged); prettier clean.

